WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.474
Hi! Circle, square, circle, square… what comes next? Today we'll find patterns with shapes.

2
00:00:09.624 --> 00:00:17.394
2D shapes include circles, squares, triangles and rectangles, plus half circles and quarter circles.

3
00:00:17.544 --> 00:00:20.682
A pattern can be about the shape changing.

4
00:00:20.832 --> 00:00:25.050
It can also be about colour, size or direction changing.

5
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:30.690
Sometimes shape and colour both change, so look carefully.

6
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:35.706
First find the group that keeps repeating. Here it's circle, square.

7
00:00:35.856 --> 00:00:38.874
Circle each group to see it clearly.

8
00:00:39.024 --> 00:00:43.146
A group can have three: circle, circle, triangle.

9
00:00:43.296 --> 00:00:47.538
Once you know the group, keep it going.

10
00:00:47.688 --> 00:00:54.018
Watch out! Some pupils only look at the first two and think it's circle, square repeating!

11
00:00:54.168 --> 00:00:59.418
Here the group is circle, square, triangle, so after a circle comes a square.

12
00:00:59.568 --> 00:01:04.074
Always find the whole repeating group first.

13
00:01:04.224 --> 00:01:14.874
Your turn! Square, triangle, square, triangle, square. What comes next? Pause and think.

14
00:01:15.024 --> 00:01:21.906
The group is square, triangle, so next is a triangle. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:22.056 --> 00:01:34.290
Another one! Circle, circle, square, circle, circle, square, circle. What comes next? Pause and think.

16
00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:43.914
The group is circle, circle, square. We're at the first circle of a new group, so next is a circle. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:44.064 --> 00:01:55.338
Here's another! Red circle, blue circle, red circle, blue circle. What comes next? Pause and think.

18
00:01:55.488 --> 00:02:04.794
The shape stays the same and the colour changes: red, blue. Next is a red circle. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:04.944 --> 00:02:16.962
Try one more! Big triangle, small triangle, big triangle, small triangle. What comes next? Pause and think.

20
00:02:17.112 --> 00:02:24.978
The size changes: big, small. Next is a big triangle. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:25.128 --> 00:02:35.802
Last one! Circle, square, triangle keeps repeating. What is the 7th shape? Pause and think.

22
00:02:35.952 --> 00:02:45.714
Each group has 3. 6 shapes make two groups, so the 7th starts a new group: a circle. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:45.864 --> 00:02:55.050
Remember: find the group that repeats and circle it. Check whether shape, colour, size or direction changes, then continue.

24
00:02:55.200 --> 00:03:00.810
Make a shape pattern with blocks or paper and test your family!

